{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Records one message and returns its id. Writes a content record (id = a hash of the text, so identical text is stored once, however many times it is said) and an occurrence record (when, who, where, pointing at the content). The only writer in the message store; every capture channel, sensor transcript and imported transcript comes through here, so downstream banks reference IDs instead of copying text.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::unique_session_id::unique_session_id;","params":[{"desc":"user | assistant | system | speaker - who produced the words.","name":"role","type":"String"},{"desc":"Where it happened: chat | room | escalation | ... . Consumers filter by venue so they never need to know which sensor produced a message.","name":"venue","type":"String"},{"desc":"The words themselves. Stored once per distinct text: the content record's id is a hash of this string, so a repeated system prompt or a repeated utterance costs nothing the second time.","name":"content","type":"String"},{"desc":"Who, when known - a voiceprint or person id for room speech, empty otherwise. Empty string, never omitted (every declared param is required).","name":"entity","type":"String"},{"desc":"How this message came to be recorded: the capturing arm, sensor kind, or importer. A tag, never a branch condition.","name":"provenance","type":"String"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"mhtnxo1a019c47805n1","readers":[],"time":1787138826298,"username":"system","writers":[]}